    "title": {
      "zh": "二进制",
      "en": "Binary"
    }
  },
  "stage": "explain",
  "title": {
    "zh": "从开关到 CPU",
    "en": "From Switches to the CPU"
  },
  "concept": {
    "zh": "二进制、位权与开关",
    "en": "Binary, place values, and switches"
  },
  "brief": {
    "zh": "用亮灯表示 1，熄灯表示 0。看每盏灯的位置如何改变它代表的数值。",
    "en": "Use a lit switch for 1 and an unlit switch for 0. See how the position of a switch changes the amount it represents."
  },
  "hints": [],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "开和关表示两种状态",
        "en": "On and off are two states"
      },
      "body": {
        "zh": "每一位只能是 0 或 1，也叫一位 bit。几位连起来可以代表更大的数。",
        "en": "Each position holds a 0 or a 1 and is called a bit. Several bits together can represent larger numbers."
      }
    },
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "每向左一位，位权翻倍",
        "en": "Double the place value at each position to the left"
      },
      "body": {
        "zh": "最右一位的位权是 1，往左是 2、4、8。把每个为 1 的位权加起来。二进制 101 等于 4 + 1，也就是 5。",
        "en": "The rightmost place is worth 1. To its left the places are worth 2, 4, and 8. Add the places with a 1. Binary 101 is 4 + 1, which is 5."
      }
    },
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "最左边的 0 可以保留",
        "en": "Keep leading zeros when a display has room"
      },
      "body": {
        "zh": "四盏灯可以显示 0101。左边的 0 不增加数值，所以它和 101 都是 5。把最左灯点亮，就会再加上 8。",
        "en": "Four switches can display 0101. The leading zero adds nothing, so it has the same value 5 as 101. Turning on the leftmost switch adds 8."
      }
    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "prompt": {
      "zh": "四盏灯从左到右是 0、1、0、1。它显示的十进制数是多少？",
      "en": "Four switches read 0, 1, 0, 1 from left to right. What decimal number do they show?"
    },
    "options": [
      {
        "zh": "3",
        "en": "3"
      },
      {
        "zh": "5",
        "en": "5"
      },
      {
        "zh": "10",
        "en": "10"
      }
    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "feedback": {
      "zh": "开着的是位权 4 和位权 1 的两盏灯。4 加 1 等于 5。",
      "en": "The places worth 4 and 1 are on. Four plus one equals 5."
    }
  },
